  "description": "Qwen3 Embedding 8B served by the already mirrored official vLLM 0.21.0 CUDA 13 OpenAI-compatible image in pooling runner mode. This active, non-default profile is a five-cell fallback for the TEI CUDA 1.9.3 profile, which supports B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000 but exits before server startup on B300/SM103. The upstream public Hugging Face metadata reports Apache-2.0 licensing, no gating, feature-extraction usage, sentence-transformers metadata, and 7,567,295,488 BF16 safetensors parameters. vLLM 0.21.0 CUDA 13 already validates B300 for the Qwen3 Embedding 0.6B pooling profile and for Qwen3 4B text generation in Forge. The 2026-05-24T21Z B300 probe started this 8B pooling profile on SM103, selected FlashInfer attention, returned HTTP 200 from /v1/embeddings, and completed 3 warmups plus 10 measured warm embedding requests. The 2026-05-24T22Z H200 probe added a non-B300 comparison cell with HTTP 200, 71.615 s startup, 111 ms warm p50, 270.27 TPS, and 95.65 GB VRAM. The 2026-05-25T00Z RTX6000 probe completed 3 warmups plus 10 measured warm embedding requests with HTTP 200, 461.069 s startup, 180 ms warm p50, 166.67 TPS, and 64.2 GB VRAM. The 2026-05-25T06Z probes completed the remaining L40S and B200 cells with HTTP 200, 646.090 s startup and 117 ms warm p50 on L40S, and 413.687 s startup and 171 ms warm p50 on B200. A 2026-05-24T22Z direct H200 full-vector parity check against the TEI CUDA 1.9.3 row compared the default manifest prompt over 4096 dimensions and measured cosine similarity 0.999952366, mean absolute difference 0.000113484, and max absolute difference 0.002169527. Keep this version non-default and non-latest because TEI remains materially cheaper on non-B300 cells even though the vLLM CUDA 13 profile now has all five current Forge GPU cells validated.",
